parts.text:
Wait — `paintMark` uses `st.aim` directly instead of `aim(st)` (which lazily defaults). If `st.aim` is null (no aim yet), the mark is hidden until a tap or first use. But I want a default centered cursor visible so users see where ЛКМ will click. Let me call `aim(st)` in paintMark — but careful: `aim()` calls `metrics()` again. Fine, but `aim(st)` assigns `st.aim` only if metrics worked. Let me use:

```js
var a = enabled ? aim(st) : st.aim, m = enabled ? metrics(st) : null;
```

Hmm, `aim(st)` when disabled would still compute. Let me write:

```js
function paintMark(st) {
  if (!st.mark) return;
  var a = st.aim;
  var m = enabled ? metrics(st) : null;
  if (enabled && !a) a = aim(st);
  ...
}
```

Simpler:

```js
  var m = enabled ? metrics(st) : null;
  var a = m ? aim(st) : null;
  if (!a || !m) { hide; return; }
```

`aim(st)` returns defaultAim if st.aim is null. Good.

Also `moveAim` uses `aim(st)` — fine.

Let me apply.

